There is no approved drug, no advanced clinical candidate and no Phase 1 candidate against {{ tract.gene | tex }} in any modality. Small-molecule tractability is not zero --- {{ tract.gene | tex }} is flagged as a druggable family with a high-quality ligand --- but it has no structure with a ligand and no high- or medium-quality pocket recorded, and nothing has been carried forward. The one modality with positive evidence beyond ligandability is the \textbf{degrader} axis, and that points the wrong way: this disease is loss of protein function, so a molecule that removes the remaining protein is the opposite of what is wanted. Direct targeting is therefore off the table. Every candidate axis below acts on something other than {{ tract.gene | tex }}: restoring protein from the nonsense allele, or reducing the downstream cost of the aneuploidy that its loss produces.
{% endif %}

