\textbf{Why these candidates are all tier 3: the tumour genotype is missing}

All five tumour-directed candidates share a single blocker, and it is the same one each time. The released data is germline whole-genome sequencing. Precision-oncology candidates are selected on the tumour's genotype --- fusion status, copy number, homologous-recombination status, aneuploidy score --- none of which is derivable from germline data. The candidates cannot be assessed, and the reason does not differ between them.

